  "textPrepSecondsInfo": "How long the network may enlarge small text on one page. It takes the smallest text first; what it has no time for is enlarged the plain way: at once, slightly lower quality. On a weak laptop \"High\" takes about 4 minutes per million pixels: a manga screenshot 20–60 s, a page covered in small text 10 minutes or more. When quality matters more than time (say, you go for a cup of tea), choose more or \"No limit\". On a graphics card the network does more in the same time.",
  "modelLines": "Text line finder (PP-OCR)",
